From: rive
Subject: [PATCH 0037] keep the memory base and bound across linear stores

A function that calls reloaded the memory base and bound from the instance
after every linear store, since nothing told LLVM a linear store cannot
write the instance. Such functions now keep them in locals refreshed after
each call, and linear, memory info and global accesses carry distinct TBAA.

